<title>USA: Transamerica to buy back stock, pay down debt.</title>
<headline>Transamerica to buy back stock, pay down debt.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transamerica Corp said Wednesday it will use proceeds from the $1.1 billion sale of its consumer lending business to pay down debt and buy back up to 6 million common shares.</p>
<p>Household International Inc said today it has agreed to buy the business for $1.1 billion in cash.</p>
<p>Transamerica said the business had a book equity of $487 million at March 31, 1997. It said it would record its gain on the sale when the deal closes.  </p>
<p>It said any gain would take into account taxes, writedowns of intangibles and the result of the continuing liquidation or sale of its remaining $280 million of special assets.</p>
</text>
